2. Configure CSV Data Set Config
In JMeter Test Plan:

Add CSV Data Set Config.

Filename: user_login_data.csv

Variable Names: username,password,endpoint

Recycle on EOF: True

Stop thread on EOF: False

Effect: Each thread reads a different row (username, password, endpoint).

3. Parameterize API Endpoint
In HTTP Request Sampler:

Method: POST

Server Name or IP: ${endpoint}

Body Data:

json
{
  "email": "${username}",
  "password": "${password}"
}
Add HTTP Header Manager:

Content-Type: application/json

4. Zomato-Style Login Flow with Correlation
Step 1: Login Request (POST).

Step 2: Add Regular Expression Extractor:

Reference Name: sessionToken

Regex: "token":"(.+?)"

Template: $1$

Step 3: Follow-up Request (Order History API):

Method: GET

URL: https://reqres.in/api/orders

Add Header: Authorization: Bearer ${sessionToken}

Effect: Demonstrates correlation — using extracted token in subsequent request.

5. Run Data-Driven Workflow
Import user_login_data.csv into JMeter.

